BBTech: Pathogen Archetypes
===========================
Basketball-to-Biotech Translation Layer | Player Archetype Catalog

Overview
--------
In BBTech, elite basketball players are encoded as biological archetypes.
Each archetype carries a biological label, a basketball phenotype, a metric suite,
and a narrative arc that maps onto real disease and systems biology concepts.
These archetypes are the canonical "organisms" of the BBTech universe.
They power Playbook simulations, Codex calculations, and agent-based experiments
inside the Digital Research Lab.

Note: All disease models are conceptual analogs used to understand complex adaptive
systems. They are not medical claims or clinical recommendations.

---

ARCHETYPE 01: Steph Curry -- Viral Archetype
--------------------------------------------
Biological Label: Virus
Basketball Phenotype: Off-dribble deep 3-point shooting, extreme range, relocation,
  conditioning, and off-ball gravity that reshapes the offensive geometry of an entire league.

Narrative Arc:
  Spillover Phase  -- Curry emerges in a mid-range/post-play ecosystem as an anomaly.
  Pandemic Phase   -- Every team must "vaccinate" (develop 3-point-centered systems) or be overwhelmed.
  Endemic Phase    -- The virus permanently rewires the league; elevated 3PA and deeper spacing become baseline.

Metric Suite:
  Infection Rate (IR)
    Definition: Rate at which teams increase 3PA and off-dribble 3PA after repeated
    exposure to Curry-style play (games, playoffs, media cycles).
    Formula: Change in 3PA per 100 possessions pre- vs. post-Curry-era exposure,
    normalized per season.

  Basic Reproduction Number (R0)
    Definition: How many new Curry-like offensive systems a single Curry-infected
    system tends to generate (coaching tree, former teammates, copycat teams).
    Formula: Count of systems whose shot profile crosses Curry-like threshold
    (deep pull-up rate + 3P share) after contact with his ecosystem.

  Viral Load (VL)
    Definition: Concentration of Curry's impact on a lineup's offensive geometry.
    Formula: Weighted composite of off-ball gravity (defender distance + help tags),
    team 3PA delta (on vs. off), and offensive rating contribution.

  Immune Escape Index (IEI)
    Definition: How often standard defensive countermeasures (traps, top-locks,
    switching) fail to suppress his eFG% and creation.
    Formula: eFG% and team ORtg vs. trap / blitz / switch coverages
    compared to league baseline.

