ARCHETYPE 02: Kyrie Irving -- Mutation Archetype
------------------------------------------------
Biological Label: Phenotypic Mutation
Basketball Phenotype: Extreme ball-handling complexity, micro-movement, touch finishing,
  and paint access as a small guard against switch-heavy, oversized defenses.

Narrative Arc:
  Pre-Kyrie small guards are unfit phenotypes in a big-wing ecosystem.
  Kyrie introduces a survival mutation: handle complexity + finishing angles allowing
  deep paint access without elite height.
  Sub-clone lineage spreads -- other guards copy complex handles, off-hand layups,
  and tight-space scoring, optimizing for pressure survival rather than distance shooting.

Metric Suite:
  Mutation Complexity Index (MCI)
    Definition: Complexity of ball-handling genome per possession.
    Formula: Weighted combination of direction changes per drive,
    speed changes per drive, and unique combo sequences per 100 possessions.

  Defensive Evasion Rate (DER)
    Definition: Probability that a primary defender is fully beaten on a possession.
    Formula: Percentage of drives resulting in primary defender displacement,
    forced help rotation, or blow-by -- relative to total on-ball possessions.

  Paint Micro-Infiltration Score (PMIS)
    Definition: Quality of paint touches by a small guard against elite rim protection.
    Formula: Frequency of paint touches per 100 possessions vs. big lineups,
    restricted-area efficiency, assist rate off paint touches.

  Adaptation Under Stress (AUS)
    Definition: Mutation success rate against playoff-level defensive treatment.
    Formula: DER and PMIS under high-pressure playoff coverages vs. regular season.

